  "readmeFile": "README.md",
  "releaseNotes": "1.5.0 - The reading surface grew a reusable session and two pieces of control: IPdfLayoutSession keeps one parse open, so the letters, the words and an export of the same pages cost one walk (the two most recent ranges are kept), PdfReadingOrderStrategy.RowBands reads a table row by row, and a page can paint in a colour space the caller names (SetFillColor/SetStrokeColor with FillPath/StrokePath). The scan allocates 5.3% less and extracts 23% colder and 15% warmer on the 200-page fixture; the endstream search and the PNG Up predictor are vectorised; a Mac-written font's MacRomanEncoding is read instead of reported, and a PAGE XML export is schema-valid. The packages are trim- and Native AOT-compatible, with the configuration-binding overload annotated as the one member outside that claim. Both legs (net10.0, net11.0) ship in one package. Details: https://github.com/MPCoreDeveloper/SharpCorePDF/blob/main/CHANGELOG.md",
